Backported drivers
==================

Copies of upstream kernel drivers that the BSP ships instead of the kernel's
own build, because the BSP needs fixes the FBOSS kernel does not carry.

Files and modules are prefixed "bp4f_" (backport for FBOSS), and each driver
registers under a "bp4f-" name, so neither the module nor the driver collides
with the kernel's version when both are installed.

bp4f_i2c_xiic.c: Linux v6.11.11 drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-xiic.c plus upstream
b7e6df2f52ed and 840d8acc8792 (SMBus block-read fixes) and the RX FIFO fix
posted to linux-i2c ("i2c: xiic: don't fail a read whose data is already in
the RX FIFO"). The header of the file lists exactly what is applied. Mirror
any new FBOSS kernel xiic patch here.
